{"date":"2026-08-23","generatedAt":1787463637519,"model":"claude-fable-5","tradingDay":false,"headline":"Gold up with long yields and a soft dollar reads as an inflation premium, not growth","body":["Exchange-traded markets were closed, so the read rests on the week and month — and it is stagflationary. Gold has risen 12.9% in a month while the 10-year yield added 8 basis points to sit at the top of its 52-week range and the 30-year gained 13. Gold climbing alongside rising yields, with the dollar index down 2.3% on the month, is the classic signature of markets demanding compensation for inflation and fiscal risk rather than pricing stronger growth.","The curve confirms it: the 30y–10y spread has steepened about 5 basis points over the month, driven by the long end — term premium, not a growth repricing. The copper/gold ratio, the cleanest growth-versus-fear gauge here, has fallen 9.5% in a month even with copper near its highs, and Brent's 6.6% weekly jump adds to the cost-pressure side of the ledger rather than the demand side.","The one dissent is bitcoin, up 21% on the week, which speaks to ample liquidity and intact risk appetite. But it still buys 2.6% fewer ounces of gold than a month ago and sits in the bottom third of its range; the hard-asset, inflation-hedge bid carries more weight than the speculative one."],"stats":{"date":"2026-08-23","tradingDay":false,"instruments":{"Bitcoin":{"last":76184.03,"tradedToday":true,"change":{"day":{"abs":-2240.5946,"pct":-2.86},"week":{"abs":13166.9566,"pct":20.89},"month":{"abs":11151.0079,"pct":17.15},"threeMonths":{"abs":-500.341,"pct":-0.65},"yearToDate":{"abs":-12179.6922,"pct":-13.78}},"range52w":{"high":124739.8109,"low":58566.092,"positionInRange":0.27},"volatility":{"annualizedPct":41.6,"vsOwnYearMedian":1.26,"regime":"normal"}},"Gold":{"last":4680.6,"tradedToday":false,"change":{"day":{"abs":164.3002,"pct":3.64},"week":{"abs":300.2001,"pct":6.85},"month":{"abs":533.7001,"pct":12.87},"threeMonths":{"abs":159.6,